[00:21.92]A legendary Chinese painting.一幅传奇的中国画作。
[00:25.47]Have you heard about a world-famous landscape painting named Dwelling in the Fuchun Mountains?你听说过那幅世界著名的山水画《富春山居图》吗？
[00:32.92]It was painted by Huang Gongwang, one of the Four Masters of the Yuan dynasty.它由元代四大家之一的黄公望所画。
[00:39.98]Many experts think it is among the greatest masterpieces in Chinese art history.许多专家认为它是中国艺术史上最伟大的杰作之一。
[00:47.40]The story behind this painting is also very unusual.这幅画背后的故事也非常特别。
[00:52.35]Huang was almost 80 years old when he began working on Dwelling in the Fuchun Mountains.黄公望开始创作《富春山居图》时，已经将近80岁了。
[01:00.44]He first made a rough drawing of the whole painting in one sitting.他先一气呵成画出了整幅画的草图。
[01:06.03]Over the following years, he then added parts to it whenever he was in the mood.在接下来的几年里，他兴致所至便会为画作添笔。
[01:12.68]The final painting was almost 7 meters long, and it was given to a friend as a present.这幅画最终长达近7米，被赠予一位朋友作为礼物。
[01:20.92]Dwelling in the Fuchun Mountains shows the beauty of the countryside of Jiangnan. 《富春山居图》展现了江南乡村的美景。
[01:27.78]The painting takes us on a breathtaking journey in the mountains.带领我们开启一场令人沉醉的山间之旅。
[01:32.88]Along the way, we follow narrow paths, cross wooden bridges, and pass along a wide river.沿途，我们循着小径前行，走过木桥，途经宽阔的河流。
[01:42.18]If we look carefully, we can see people far away in the landscape.若仔细观察，便能看到山水间远处的人影。
[01:48.59]Some woodsmen are hidden among the trees.一些樵夫隐匿在树林中。
[01:52.49]On the river, there is a man sitting alone on a boat.河面上，有一位男子独自坐在船上。
[01:57.65]He is fishing.他正在垂钓。
[01:59.43]It looks like he is at one with nature, and we feel the same when we look at the painting.他仿佛与自然融为一体，我们观赏画作时也能感受到这份和谐。
[02:06.75]Dwelling in the Fuchun Mountains was such an amazing painting that it was copied by hundreds of artists.《富春山居图》如此精妙，引得数百位艺术家纷纷临摹。
[02:15.23]The original painting changed owners many times.真迹曾多次易主。
[02:19.62]One of the owners liked it so much that he even put it next to himself while sleeping and eating.有一位藏家对它钟爱至极，甚至在吃饭、睡觉时都将其放在身边。
[02:27.21]Sometime around 1650, something terrible happened.大约在1650年左右，一件不幸的事发生了。
[02:33.32]The famous painting was damaged by fire, and it was split into two pieces.这幅名画在火灾中受损，被分成了两部分。
[02:40.26]The two parts went their separate ways.这两部分从此天各一方。
[02:44.14]In the following centuries, they each experienced many dramatic events.在接下来的几个世纪里，它们各自经历了许多跌宕起伏的故事。
[02:50.24]One of them even became part of the Qianlong emperor's art collection.其中一部分甚至被纳入乾隆皇帝的收藏。
[02:55.43]In 2011, after more than 300 years of separation, the two parts of the legendary painting were at last shown together in one exhibition.2011年，在分离300多年后，这幅传奇画作的两部分终于在同一场展览中重逢。


